Role::AsyncHTTP builds Net::Async::HTTP->new with defaults (pipeline => 1, max_connections_per_host => 1). With 3+ concurrent requests on one engine over a keep-alive connection, NaHTTP pipelines queued requests behind an in-flight one; cancelling any request (caller cancel, or the k194 abort after a chunk-sub die) closes the connection and fails the pipelined siblings with "Connection closed". For LLM streaming, pipelining buys little (head-of-line blocking behind a long stream). Decide whether to build the client with pipeline => 0 (and/or a higher max_connections_per_host); needs a keep-alive test daemon (t/lib/Test/LocalHTTPDaemon.pm forces Connection: close). Reproduced in k194 fix round 1 with a scratch keep-alive HTTP::Daemon.

